I propose blueprints for NetHack because I've been wasting excruciating 
amounts of time playing Arcanum instead of NetHack. In Arcanum a 
technologist can use a schematic to create a powerful weapon.

For NetHack, a blueprint could tell a player how to make their own 
special items. For very little gruntwork, a blueprint could simply be a 
spoiler that lets a greenhorn player know "enchant armor + dragon scales 
= dragon scale mail".

Something a little more involved, for example, "+2 longsword + lit potion 
of oil = firebrand" or "blessed magic lantern + +2 longsword = sunsword". 
Implement a #combine command for this feature. Of course they'd need the 
blueprint to do it. I chose +2 enchantment because I don't think any 
character class starts out with a +2 longsword even though there are a 
few which start with a +1 longsword.

A blueprint would simply be a (gelatinous cube not floating eye) blue 
question mark which would be randomly generated via death drop, found in 
bookstores or in tool shops.

As for potions, I am sure that someone has already brought up the idea. 
Green potions have a chance of generating a green slime much like a milky 
potion generates a ghost. Black potions would have black puddings, blue 
potions would make blue jellies and so forth.


